WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:03.341
Spring is the season of new beginnings.

2
00:00:03.342 --> 00:00:07.881
Flowers and trees come back to life after the long winter.

3
00:00:07.882 --> 00:00:13.810
Spring is also the time to celebrate Easter.

4
00:00:13.811 --> 00:00:17.577
For Christians, Easter is a religious holiday.

5
00:00:17.578 --> 00:00:22.260
Christians believe Jesus rose from the dead three days after he was killed.

6
00:00:22.261 --> 00:00:30.232
Easter is a holiday to celebrate Jesus' resurrection.

7
00:00:30.233 --> 00:00:35.404
Today, however, Christians are not the only people who celebrate Easter.

8
00:00:35.405 --> 00:00:38.111
Where does the word "Easter" come from?

9
00:00:38.112 --> 00:00:43.954
What do the bunnies and eggs have to do with Easter?

10
00:00:43.955 --> 00:00:47.932
The word "Easter" comes from a goddess named Eostre.

11
00:00:47.933 --> 00:00:51.880
Ancient people held a festival to worship Eostre every spring.

12
00:00:51.881 --> 00:00:57.274
Her symbol was a rabbit.

13
00:00:57.275 --> 00:01:02.415
Eostre, or Easter, and the rabbit both symbolize fertility.

14
00:01:02.416 --> 00:01:06.249
Fertility means having lots and lots of babies.

15
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:12.591
So the Easter rabbit represents new life.

16
00:01:12.592 --> 00:01:16.481
The egg is also a symbol of fertility and new life.

17
00:01:16.482 --> 00:01:20.904
There are many customs and traditions associated with eggs.

18
00:01:20.905 --> 00:01:29.196
Some cultures even believe that the Earth hatched from a giant egg!

19
00:01:29.197 --> 00:01:32.122
Easter eggs are painted bright colors.

20
00:01:32.123 --> 00:01:38.966
These colors represent spring.

21
00:01:38.967 --> 00:01:42.446
In Greece, Easter eggs are colored red.

22
00:01:42.447 --> 00:01:45.135
Red represents Jesus' blood.

23
00:01:45.136 --> 00:01:50.219
In some parts of Germany and Austria, people color their eggs green.

24
00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:58.262
In Russia and Ukraine, people decorate their eggs in beautiful patterns with gold and silver.

25
00:01:58.263 --> 00:02:03.010
On Easter day some countries have egg-rolling competitions.

26
00:02:03.011 --> 00:02:05.927
The egg that rolls the farthest wins.

27
00:02:05.928 --> 00:02:12.837
But the most popular Easter game is the Easter egg hunt.

28
00:02:12.838 --> 00:02:18.965
Children believe the Easter Bunny brings the eggs during the night.

29
00:02:18.966 --> 00:02:23.004
On Easter morning, the children look for the eggs.

30
00:02:23.005 --> 00:02:27.680
Sometimes there is a prize for the child who finds the most eggs.

31
00:02:27.681 --> 00:02:31.926
Everyone has a good time.

32
00:02:31.927 --> 00:02:35.049
Easter is a fun time for the whole family.

33
00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:40.857
It is a time to celebrate life.

